<h2>Command Collection</h2>
<p>We have gathered the commands you use often at a glance, with a note on what each one actually does. Slash commands are written in the namespaced (<code>/oh-my-claudecode:</code>) form wherever possible.</p>

<div class="tbl-wrap">
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr><th>Category</th><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>Install</td><td><code>/plugin marketplace add &lt;repo&gt;</code> → <code>/plugin install oh-my-claudecode</code></td><td>Registers the plugin repository, then installs OMC. Run the two lines in order.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Project setup</td><td><code>/oh-my-claudecode:omc-setup --local</code></td><td>Creates OMC settings that apply only to the current project. It does not touch the global settings.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Global setup</td><td><code>/oh-my-claudecode:omc-setup</code></td><td>Creates settings that apply commonly to every project. It may affect your existing global CLAUDE.md.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Diagnosis</td><td><code>/oh-my-claudecode:omc-doctor</code></td><td>Checks the install and configuration state and tells you if something is wrong. The first step in troubleshooting.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Project documentation</td><td><code>/oh-my-claudecode:deepinit [path]</code></td><td>Analyzes the project structure and organizes it into a document (AGENTS.md) that is easy for AI to understand.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Requirement clarification</td><td><code>/deep-interview &lt;idea&gt;</code></td><td>Throws questions at a vague idea to refine it into concrete requirements.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Autonomous implementation</td><td><code>/oh-my-claudecode:autopilot &lt;task&gt;</code></td><td>Takes the requirements and proceeds on its own from implementation through verification.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Carry through to the end</td><td><code>/oh-my-claudecode:ralph &lt;task&gt;</code></td><td>Repeats without stopping until the completion condition is satisfied.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Maximum parallelism</td><td><code>/oh-my-claudecode:ultrawork &lt;task&gt;</code> or <code>ulw</code></td><td>Handles several mutually independent tasks at the same time to increase speed.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Team execution</td><td><code>/oh-my-claudecode:team &lt;N&gt;:&lt;agent&gt; &lt;task&gt;</code></td><td>Assigns the role (agent) to the specified number (N) of agents and divides the work among them.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Update</td><td><code>/plugin marketplace update omc</code> → <code>/oh-my-claudecode:omc-setup</code></td><td>Syncs the marketplace to the latest, then applies the settings again.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Plan / consensus</td><td><code>/oh-my-claudecode:plan</code> · <code>/oh-my-claudecode:ralplan</code></td><td>Lays out an execution plan before the work. ralplan reviews more carefully, on a consensus basis. (omc-plan is a compatibility alias for plan)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Cancel</td><td><code>/oh-my-claudecode:cancel</code> or <code>stopomc</code> / <code>cancelomc</code></td><td>Stops the OMC work in progress.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Pattern extraction</td><td><code>/oh-my-claudecode:skillify</code></td><td>Extracts a work pattern that was effective in a session into a reusable skill. (learner is a deprecated alias)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>HUD setup</td><td><code>/oh-my-claudecode:hud setup</code></td><td>Sets up the on-screen display (HUD) that shows the progress of the work.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">How to read this</span>
    The parts wrapped in angle brackets, like <code>&lt;task&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;idea&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;N&gt;</code>, are slots you replace with actual values. For example, in the <code>&lt;task&gt;</code> slot you write the work to be done, such as "implement the login API". Parts wrapped in square brackets, like <code>[path]</code>, are optional items you may omit.
</div>
